  description: Antimony is a chemical element with symbol Sb (from Latin:stibium)
    and atomic number 51. A lustrous gray metalloid, it is found in nature mainly
    as the sulfide mineral stibnite (Sb2S3). Antimony compounds have been known since
    ancient times and were used for cosmetics; metallic antimony was also known,
    but it was erroneously identified as lead upon its discovery.
